/forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T20:25:37-07:00","id":556426,"title":"","content":"&quot;Don't you just love it when you don't have to fight.&quot; Amelia will also search for the scepter but will also try to keep the guardian in sight just in case. <br /> <br /> Amelia scores <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/7973/view\" target=\"_blank\">zero</a> success","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T20:48:15-07:00","id":556439,"title":"","content":"Jensven starts his morning by breaking his fast sharing venison and oats with Shadow, &quot;Eat up, Shadow. I don't know when we will be able to eat as good as this for a while. We are going someplace dangerous and I wouldn't trust the demons to have food ready for us.&quot; He then commandeers a kitchen and renders down venison, mutton, and various local plants in a large pot filled with water. The Lightbringer lets it boil down until there is nearly no liquid in it. After letting it cool just enough, he forms it into small dabs and cakes. He then bakes it on low heat until it is dry, compact, and not burnt. All through the process of preparing this special food for the dog, Shadow will poke his head into the kitchen, but stay well away from the heat. As payment for allowing him to use the kitchen, Jensven leaves the food that he didn't use in his cooking.<br /> <br /> The Dawn will then go to a forge and purchase some of the best stoking fuel he can find. Cinder will need fuel and he was determined to get him something special to keep him going. Jensven also makes sure he picks up various grades of wood and coal, just to give the little ball of fire some variety.<br /> <br /> His next stop is to make sure that he has plenty of water skins. It would not do to have anyone overheat when going through the large desert that Yi mentioned, especially Shadow. A sled or a cart would be impractical in the sand, so he arranged for Shadow to have saddlebags of the sort a small pony would wear. These he filled with a rough blanket and a couple water skins. Jensven himself had a pack and other types of straps and things that would allow him to carry the rest of what he, Shadow, and Cinder would need for the trip to the city of demons. Getting back would be the trick.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the Sword of Heaven sits kneels down next to the canine and combs out his coat. He pulls many tufts of downy fur from under the coarse hair that protects Shadow from the elements. Humming while he takes care of his companion, the Ascending Sun soon finds that he has a pile of fur nearly the size of the dog when he is finished with the brushing.<br /> <br /> Having finished the preparations needed for his companions, he checks the three swords he has with him and his chain shirt for any defects and corrects the minor dings, rust spots, and pits that he finds.<br /> <br /> Only after going to all this trouble to make sure things are as ready as he would need them to be does he head off to the Artificery to find Cinder, a nice block of hardwood in hand.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I am going to be rolling to see if I can make the puppy chow just in case it is needed. This is a Craft (Water) roll I believe. So I have to use Perception (3) + Craft (Water) 0 for a total of three (3) dice and <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/7974/view\" target=\"_blank\">one success.</a> I guess that means I just barely make the food edible. Good thing. I don't want to kill the dog. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":1146,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","user":"Belkra","date":". 06-15-2015, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T21:30:36-07:00","id":557814,"title":"","content":"Tirin will scour the pile herself, her eyes becoming like those of the peregrine falcon for a split second.<br /> <br /> She rolls Perception, having no training in investigation. She rolls <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8028/view\" target=\"_blank\"> 2 suxx </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T14:43:11-07:00","id":558766,"title":"","content":"(Wyld)<br /> <br /> Our heroes' search for the Scepter of Aurem bears no fruit, until Tirien hears faint sounds of crying. Following the noise, you find a shallow slit in the wall that a person can barely fit through. Claw marks score the wall so thickly that they begin to blur together. <br /> <br /> Glancing through the slit, our heroes see a slight, young looking woman, who seems human to all outward appearance. She is hunched over, shuddering with fear, and grasping a long, heavy, sapphire-capped gilt rod.<br /> <br /> What do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:04:48-07:00","id":560782,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Seeing the woman in such a condition Amelia wants to go see her </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">inside, but one</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> glance at the slit and her somewhat bulky armor and she knows she doesn't fit. She removes her helmet which simply folds in on itself and</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">disappears</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> in an impossible manner in the collar of her armor, she also put aside her weapon so that she would not be too intimidating or menacing. Using the most caring tone she can Amelia will try to see if the woman is able to speak or if her mind is too much consumed by fear to communicate.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hello are you hurt ?&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:57:58-07:00","id":561231,"title":"","content":"Saffron stays back, watching. If the woman isn't what she appears, it's best to let a more experienced swordswoman handle it. Or at least that's how he'll justify himself to her if something goes wrong. Truth is, he'd rather be a little farther from the blast zone. How on earth would a delicate specimen of loveliness wind up here? &quot;Milady, this one would like to warn you that around these lands a beautiful flower may hide poison.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T15:18:52-07:00","id":561271,"title":"","content":"Yi had returned to the temple of Originese after his conversation with Jensven, but not joined Larissa as he normally did. Instead he prostrated himself before the altar of Origenese, after the evening prayer was completed and said. <br /> <br /> &quot;Oh god, my grandfather, who has taken me into your city, your house, and your family: Let it not be said I came to you uncivilized, that I was ignorant of xenia and what is owed a stranger to his host. I swore an oath that I should pay back all you offered and so shall it be, and Heaven I call to witness. Yet now I must go forth from your city and return again after many days. That all men and gods may know my faithfulness now I shall go from this place and prepare for you the first payment of what is due you. As it was long ago, so shall it be again; the word of the Lawgiver shall be held most highly exalted.&quot;<br /> <br /> So saying he turned and walked away, not to return till he had seen Malfeas' viridian sun and felt the hate of the Demon Emperor scouring decadence from his flesh. His steps took him through dusty streets. Once or twice a footpad or ruffian stepped from shadow to bar his way. The first threw herself to the ground chanting &quot;Namo Zhinan&quot;. Some knelt awkwardly. Most found other streets to menace. Once he heard a scuffle a street over, and shouting of &quot;the priest&quot; but there was nothing but bloodstains when he reached it to investigate. In such fashion he reached the river.<br /> <br /> Silently he walked down, the water rising up to his ankles, then his knees, then his waist. Slowly, deliberately, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X4L2EUPM6Dc\" target=\"_blank\">he began to sing on old song</a>. He had first heard it long, long ago. When he had been a sun dark boy still lost in the halls of the academy. He had never seen the summoning, only heard it echoing through the ancient halls. It had seemed... forbidden then. Like a part of the world that was secret and not meant for him. Yet it had also excited him. The world was richer and more wondrous than he had ever imagined. All those feelings welled up again as he sun.<br /> <br /> The sun descended in the sky. The mist rose over the river and the solar shivered beneath his sodden robes. When the golden disk was half obscured he opened his eyes and brought the jade staff down to strike the surface of the water. A single, perfect, ripple spread from the spot glowing as it grew. In the sudden darkness the golden mark on his brow hung in the air like a will o wisp. Yet there were other lights.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ainti Teph, it has been a long time. I don't suppose Lookshy's pact with your court still applies to me, or that the arrangement of being summoned to do as thou wilt will be acceptable.&quot;<br /> <br /> He saw her shape, reclining on the water with more grace than many a courtesan on silken pillows. He knew she was beautiful, and that she enjoyed being thought as such.<br /> <br /> &quot;Now I, being poor, have nothing but a contest to propose. I saw once, when you and mistress Arada wove together, she at her loom and you where the many threaded river was woven into the sea. So I propose this. We will each weave a bolt, and you may decide which is the better. If you judge mine superior you will weave the blessing of cool water upon it as you did for General Karal before the Southern Campaign. If yours is superior I will serve you by the same submission as your kind often serves mine. I shall let Heaven judge your honesty, and the name the five gods who love me to witness. Are these terms acceptable, or shall our wills contest instead?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>If it comes to a clash of wills</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8131/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8131/view</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8132/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.rpnation.com/styles/rpnlogo12.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8132/view\" target=\"_blank\"> Oops! We ran into some problems. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8132/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8132/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8133/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.rpnation.com/styles/rpnlogo12.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8133/view\" target=\"_blank\"> Oops! We ran into some problems. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8133/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8133/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8134/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8134/view</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>If she accepts the offer</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yi placed his left hand against the surface of the water, the tips of his fingers just barely touching the black surface. With careful motions, more gentle than a musician upon his strings, he began to upset the surface. Each little ripple, thin as thread, was caught by another finger until he had begun to draw them from the water like strands of gossamer. Lifting his hand up as though handing them to another they caught and began to slowly twist, spun by the wheel of the turning heavens.<br /> <br /> Then he raised his right hand, weaving his fingers between the stars. Deep, deep, purple came away, the darkness between the stars on which the constellations were hung. This he fixed to the wheel of the turning earth, for why should the heavens think they and not the ever changing earth moves? Only the keenest eyes could see the fibers rising ever thinner into the sky.<br /> <br /> He repeated the process and then repeated it again. When they had grown long, long enough to bind a strong man so that he strained but could not break them, he began to spin. It was not dance, not as the teachers of dance or the professionals who made their living on the stage would recognize it. He spun and spun and spun, and his robes whirled about him like a cloud. It was not excessively fast or frantic. As he spun he let go of his worries about what he had done and what he was soon to do. He stopped caring about his position or his image. He spun on, and thought of gratitude and excellence in remembrance of the sun.<br /> <br /> When he at last came to a stop the cloth lay spread about him on the water and the scene he had woven into it as at last apparent. Water and mist, sky and shadow, it showed the shore and the city and the stars about the moon. On the shoulders of the Exalted it would show silver sands and black towers, bowed kings and kneeling lords, white cities and golden temples. Black as night and smoke and water beneath the sea, flashing with the infinite shades of darkness, glittering as though spun from ten thousand jewels. A black mirror in woven form, to show all and none of all that would ever surround it.<br /> <br /> Yi did not speak, but turned to the elemental to see her response.<br /> <br /> Int/Per/Dex 5 + Craft 5<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8135/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.rpnation.com/styles/rpnlogo12.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8135/view\" target=\"_blank\"> Oops! We ran into some problems. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8135/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8135/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Stunt<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8136/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.rpnation.com/styles/rpnlogo12.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8136/view\" target=\"_blank\"> Oops! We ran into some problems. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8136/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8136/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Second Craft Excellency for 5 successes:<br /> <br /> Total: 11 successes<br /> <br /> Using CNNT to speed things up and Sunlit anvil forging practice for material.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:42:51-07:00","id":562552,"title":"","content":"(Wyld) <br /> <br /> The young woman looks up with red-rimmed eyes, an expression of surprise and hope on her face. <br /> <br /> &quot;I'm o-o-kay,&quot; she sniffs, an oddly harmonic lilt to her voice, &quot;But how did you get past the monster? Did you kill it?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T21:06:48-07:00","id":562600,"title":"","content":"(Jensven)<br /> <br /> Your cooking results in thick canvas bag filled with baked dog-food (though it is equally edible to humans I suppose). The chefs in the kitchen find your foodstuff to be a bit odd, but they file it away for future reference. Baked meat-and-vegetable balls? Could be good for the soldiers. Might want to bake them into loafs, though. Less work that making the individual balls, after all. <br /> <br /> Procuring the fuel is slightly more difficult, but you obtain a fair amount of wood, charcoal, and even a bit of coal. <br /> <br /> Heading into the Artificery, you are met with an unusual degree of activity. There are easily more people here at once than there were for the entirety of your previous visits. A half-dozen master smiths work at their individual forges, each with several apprentices and a journeyman or two, orbiting them, assisting where able. <br /> <br /> And, at Cinder's forge, you see Maia working alone as she shapes a heavy polearm, made entirely iron, She seems to sculpt both metal and flame with her bare hands; aside from looking as if she just spent a long morning in the sun, she seems unaffected by the fires around her. Cinder's head(?) bobs around her, prattling on and on about a dozen topics, only one of which is Maia's current project.<br /> <br /> Seeing Jensven, Cinder flits over like a wayward ember. &quot;You're back! You know, you're the only one here I can talk to! Everyone else just ignores me, you know? When are we going on that trip? Is that for me?&quot; Cinder asks with all of the energy of a sugar-crazed five-year-old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T23:26:36-07:00","id":562702,"title":"","content":"(Yi)<br /> <br /> &quot;The Weaver of Waters and Wishes answers your call, Exalted One,&quot; Ainti Teph says with a small nod. Meeting Yi's eyes she continues, &quot;You are exiled from Lookshy, and have been declared Anathema; your name has been excised from the rolls of those who may call upon the service of me and mine at will. But your contest entreagues me, and I shall permit this minor indiscretion. &quot;<br /> <br /> Yi can see the hunger in her eyes, orbs as green and deep as the inland sea. It is not the contest that has caught her attention.<br /> <br /> It was the prize. <br /> <br /> With the terms of the contest set, the water spirit pulls out her shuttle of blackest jade and sends it soaring unto the heavens. When the shuttle returns, it brings with it a wine-dark thunderhead, crackling with yellow-blue lightning. She uses not her fingers to weave her cloth; tiny jets of water from the river shoot the shuttle through the cloud. The jets knock the jade artifact though the cloud up and down, side to side, fore and aft, and all directions in between with such speed that the heavy weaver's tool becomes little more than a narrow blur. Some of the jets are caught in the tightening cloud. You can tell this is no error, but instead a deliberate part of the construction. The rhythmic sound of the jets, the crackling of the lightning and the whir of the shuttle combine to form an almost musical quality. <br /> <br /> A long bolt of cloth sits before you, woven of still-vapor cloud. Long stands of still-liquid water run through it in slowly swirling patterns, contrasted with the sharp flashing patterns of trapped lightning. Combined, you get the impression that the water-spirit had taken a hurricane and made a scarf from it. <br /> <br /> With both parties finished, Ainti Teph examines the products. Both pieces are subject to all manner of testing its quality. Given the degree of her examination you are half surprised when she places both bolts down without tasting them. With a wicked grin on her face, the water spirit declares, &quot;As the judge of this contest, I declare that my craft is-&quot;<br /> <br /> Ainti Teph is cut off when a short dark figure seems to condense from the mist and places a slender hand upon her shoulder. You hear a soft murmur echo from the new arrival, and the water spirit's face pales and her eyes grow shocked.<br /> <br /> &quot;- is inferior. Definitely inferior. I lost.&quot; Ainti Teph blurts out. The figure removes its hand and seems to fade back into the mist with that, but you get the feeling that whomever, or whatever, it is is still watching. <br /> <br /> The water spirit holds up her end of the bargain and places the desired charm upon your cloth. once she has done so, Ainti Teph says, &quot;I will not tell anyone of this meeting, Exalted One. But never call me again if you relish the freedom you have from the Seventh Legion.&quot;<br /> <br /> She stands tall and straight as she declares her term of service fulfilled. And with that, she is gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T06:28:50-07:00","id":562935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=562552#post562552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Wyld)<br /> <br /> The young woman looks up with red-rimmed eyes, an expression of surprise and hope on her face.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm o-o-kay,&quot; she sniffs, an oddly harmonic lilt to her voice, &quot;But how did you get past the monster? Did you kill it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hearing her voice remind her of Teleri when he spoke. a fae sent to steal the scepter could make sense that aurem could have sent someone else or he spoke that a sacrifice was sent with the egg. <br /> &quot;No it's not but it's not gonna attack us for now, so who are you and what are you doing here ?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T09:11:49-07:00","id":563065,"title":"","content":"&quot;I doubt Larissa has such pule, that Aesculapius would risk such for me even with the temple I have built him, or that Ibsha Lahar with whom once I lay would even know from so casual an invocation, and the King of Heaven would expect me to lose or support me if I was foolish enough to do so. Do I then have the honor of addressing my grandfather, or has what little I have done and what little more I have promised beneath the endless sky raised my poor person to the notice of so great a divinity?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T11:12:09-07:00","id":563119,"title":"","content":"Jensven gives Maia the kind of respectful, professional nod he had seen the Guild smiths give each other during his short stay with them. It wouldn't do to give any impression that something that hadn't happened was happening. Besides, the forge-mistress is at work, and he doesn't want to disturb her. If she is constructing such a weapon, it has to be for someone of import. The smith turned Solar enjoyed watching other smiths work nearly as much as he enjoyed doing the forging himself. He doubts he would ever be able to sculpt fire like that, but if he looks closely there was something he could learn about forge-craft. Observe he does. He knows he could use the new powers he was given by the sun to increase his ability to focus his sight, but he holds that in check. He doesn't want to use such things frivolously. It seems a waste.<br /> <br /> Shadow has other ideas. To the dog, Maia is someone to be pounced on, licked, and greeted with a blur of the tail. He gets as close as he dares whines and makes noises that sound like he is attempting to imitate mortal speech. It is obvious the flames scare him, but he is insistent on getting the attention of the woman in front of him.<br /> <br /> The Dawn turns to the equally hyper forge spirit, &quot;Yes, Cinder. The wood is for you. I thought you could use it as a resting place while we were traveling. That is, if you are able to rest in it and not burn it up. I also bought various other kinds of wood, charcoal, and coal for you to eat when you are away. You do need to eat, right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":1146,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","user":"Belkra","date":". 06-21-2015, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:02:17-07:00","id":564322,"title":"","content":"(Wyld)<br /> <br /> The woman sniffs and rubs her nose. She gains some small measure of composure as she says, &quot;My name is Quickly Falls The Silverleaf. My parents have drank of the powers of the Bloodfire, and my mother sits upon the Hundredfold Council of Moxe-Ulto. I was kidnapped by Yttrus in one of his raids on my homeland. I was told that all I had to do was take an egg down here and I would be let go.&quot; <br /> <br /> The recollection of the events that brought her here causes the young woman to lose what little composure she had, &quot;And then the egg hatched and a giant monster came out and it chased me over here and tried to eat me...&quot;<br /> <br /> Anything further is cut off by a return of the crying that led you here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T13:49:39-07:00","id":564511,"title":"","content":"(Yi)<br /> <br /> &quot;You sound like Serapis when he's drunk,&quot; whispers a feminine voice from no discernible direction, &quot;And Helios always.&quot;<br /> <br /> Once again, a figure seems to condense from the mist, this time right in front of Yi. The figure is short and cowled, and covered in loose clothing of a dark grey or blue that disguise the lines of their figure, though Yi can notice a slight flair to their hips and chest, hinting at a feminine form beneath.<br /> <br /> &quot;I have no name in this age, though in the First I was called Zorya Serenitor, 'Who Cleanses The Skies',&quot; the figure says softly, &quot;the Sun has decided to pay attention to this place, in his own way. Where the gaze of the Most High falls, my siblings and I go.&quot; You detect a hint of amusement in her voice as she continues,&quot; I was in the neighborhood, so your call to Heaven called me here. As is my nature.&quot;<br /> <br /> Zorya begins to fade back into the mist, saying &quot;I will not help you otherwise, for that too is my nature.&quot;<br /> <br /> Zorya disappears into the mist, her form and presence gone, leaving Yi seemingly alone the banks of the river. Then he feels a hand grip onto his shoulder, softly but firmly.<br /> <br /> &quot;Be careful,&quot; Zorya whispers into Yi's ear, &quot;his heart still breaks whenever one of you falls.&quot;<br /> <br /> The hand releases Yi's shoulder, and when he turns around there is nothing there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 06-22-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:33:26-07:00","id":564656,"title":"","content":"(Jensven)<br /> <br /> &quot;Huh? No, I don't need to eat,&quot; Cinder starts before Maia whistles. Cinder head back over to her, where he consumes the heat from Maia's polearm. At the end, the weapon, which had been glowing from the heat to which it had been exposed, is drawing in condensation, while Cinder's flame turns blue-white with only traces of his usual orange coloration at the tips of his flame. <br /> <br /> &quot;Where was I?&quot; he says as he bobs back, &quot;Oh, yeah. I don't need to eat. Or do anything even a little bit like what you people with bodies do. It's weird I tell you. Just weird. But burning things helps me regain my energy if I exert myself. Don't need to. But it helps.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:42:39-07:00","id":565345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=564322#post564322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Wyld)<br /> <br /> The woman sniffs and rubs her nose. She gains some small measure of composure as she says, &quot;My name is Quickly Falls The Silverleaf. My parents have drank of the powers of the Bloodfire, and my mother sits upon the Hundredfold Council of Moxe-Ulto. I was kidnapped by Yttrus in one of his raids on my homeland. I was told that all I had to do was take an egg down here and I would be let go.&quot;<br /> <br /> The recollection of the events that brought her here causes the young woman to lose what little composure she had, &quot;And then the egg hatched and a giant monster came out and it chased me over here and tried to eat me...&quot;<br /> <br /> Anything further is cut off by a return of the crying that led you here.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If we get you out of here can you give me that ?&quot; Amelia points the scepter with her armored finger.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T14:13:29-07:00","id":565746,"title":"","content":"&quot;Good. I hope I have enough then,&quot; The swordsman starts. &quot;I came to get you for our journey. That is if you can come after all. I would understand if you need to be here, or if you need to see to some things before you go.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Dawn retrieves his noisy companion by lifting the animal bodily around the legs, &quot;Maia is working, boy. You can tackle her when we get back.&quot; Being suspended and not able to touch the ground is clearly disconcerting for the dog and it immediately falls still and quiet.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, Cinder. If you need to stay here for a little longer, I might be able to help out. What do you say? I'm ready to get going when you are, but if I have to wait, I might as well make myself useful.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T21:27:40-07:00","id":567356,"title":"","content":"&quot;This strikes me as something of a trap. You, girl, what year is it?&quot; Tirien asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:28:47-07:00","id":567997,"title":"","content":"(Wyld) <br /> <br /> &quot;Wha?&quot; The woman says to Amelia, &quot;Yes, of course. I'm only holding on to it 'cause the monster's scared of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> She cocks her head in response to Tirien's question. &quot;It's year 46 of the eleventh age, of course.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:58:36-07:00","id":568047,"title":"","content":"(Jensven)<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh! Okay,&quot; Cinder says. He flits over to Maia, who is putting down the weapon she was working on. Cinder's fire becomes very straight and steady, almost as if he is standing up straight. He leads his throat, saying, &quot;Madame Thaumaturge, as per the details of our contract, I declare my term of service complete.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maia nods, a small frown on her face. Cinder continues on, saying, &quot;if I don't make it back, I want you to know you've been just like a mother to me. A crabby old mother who needs to get out of the house more often-&quot;<br /> <br /> Maia's prosthetic arm slams into the tiny fire-ball, sending him flying across the room. &quot;Your jokes stink,&quot; she says, her voice cracking. &quot;Make it back safely, you hear? Both of you. Alright,&quot; she amends after a sharp bark from Shadow, &quot;All three of you. Make it back.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cinder laughs as he flies to the top of the room and releases a massive disk of fire, drawing all eyes in the room to himself. &quot;You her that,&quot; he says with a manic laugh in his voice, &quot;You can't rely on me to do your work for you! Good luck dealing with Methis!&quot;<br /> <br /> The tiny fire-spirit. Now returned to his normal coloration, lights down on the wood Jensven brought. He spreads over nearly half the wood, but remains a respectful distance from Jensven's hand. &quot;We leaving, or what?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T14:30:20-07:00","id":569603,"title":"","content":"As Cinder is hovering over to Jensven, the Dawn has to release an increasingly distressed canine that is loosing his cool because of the little talking fire that is headed directly for him. Shadow scampers some distance away from the fire, but grows curious when the flame settles near his exalted companion without harming him. The neatly groomed animal cautiously pads over to stand as near to Jensven as he dares. It is still further than usual, but it seems the animal is at least at ease with the current situation as it stands.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll bring both of these guys back for you, Maia. You have a bone ready for Shadow and a nice little cozy fireplace for Cinder. They'll likely want to rest and relax after this.&quot; Jensven seems likely to add more, but decides against it.<br /> <br /> As he starts to head out with his furry friend in tow, he continues to Cinder, &quot;Yeah, we're getting out of here. We have to see Yi first and then he will take us to where we have to go. Well, him or one of his other allies. You know, we are going to do a big favor for Originese. It might even get you a little respect around here after being part of our little expedition. Hey, are you able to go in the block, or do I have to hold you like this the whole time?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T14:31:58-07:00","id":573182,"title":"","content":"(Jensven)<br /> <br /> &quot;I can move myself, if that's what you're asking,&quot; Cinder, says, hopping off the log like an errant ember. He flits around a bit before settling back down. &quot;Truth be told, it would just be easier if I Rode with you or your cow. I mean dog.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T19:56:22-07:00","id":573489,"title":"","content":"The Dawn starts on his way to meet up with Yi, &quot;You don't mean ride by merging with the person or animal, do you?&quot; He leaves the Artificery and soon the Academy as he chats in the general direction of the flame. &quot;I'm not so sure I would go for that, for me or Shadow. Especially, if this would give you any sort of control over either of us.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T09:27:13-07:00","id":574028,"title":"","content":"(Jensven)<br /> <br /> &quot;Put your hand up here,&quot; Cinder sighs, &quot;I need to put a palm in my face.&quot;<br /> <br /> Even if Jensven were inclined to let Cinder face-Palm himself by proxy, he does not get the opportunity. The fire-spirit shoots into the air and begins his enthusiastic bobbing and flitting that is his analog to talking with his hands.<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay. To start, like, ninety-nine percent of those stories you hear about baleful gods and demons and ghosts controlling the bodies of unwitting people are complete fabrications. Or maybe three quarters,&quot; Cinder amends, &quot;Half. Half of them are fabrications. That's as low as I'm going. Half.<br /> <br /> &quot;Anyways, the point is that you people are way too focused on that meaty bag you live in for a few decades. You know it uses a derivation of burning to get the Fire essence required to stay in motion? And a really inefficient one at that. Why can't you just burn your food? You'll get more out of it, and can eat a much wider variety of foodstuffs. Where was I? Oh. Yeah. Meat-bags.<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay. For the sake of this conversation, let's imagine that the bag of muddy water you're irrationally attached to is a boat. No, a cart. Carts are better. So, your body is a cart, right? Now, attach a dog to pull it. I mean a cow. What's the difference between a dog and a cow anyway? The guy who taught me this said that cows are four-legged hairy animals. Dogs are four-legged hairy animals too. Why do you even need more than one word for a four-legged hairy animals? I'm getting away from the point. Your muddy-water cart has a cow. That's your animal soul. 'Cause it's represented by an animal in the metaphor. Simile. Analogy? Whatever. The animal soul is what does all the work of pulling your body around and making it do things and stuff. <br /> <br /> &quot;Now, give your mud-cart and non-descript hairy animal soul a driver. That's the higher soul, because it sits up higher on the cart than the hairy animal soul. That's the part of you that does all of your thinking and talking and whatever, and becomes a ghost or goes to your next body whenever the mud-cart you're in now breaks down. It holds the reigns to your animal soul and tells it what to do, where to go and stuff. With me so far?&quot;<br /> <br /> Cinder halts his tirade for a moment, but launches back into it before Jensven has a chance to answer. &quot;So, spiritual riding is basically like me hoping into the back of your cart. I could try to wrestle the reigns of your cow soul from you, but lets face it, you're way stronger than me and your driver soul would tie me up and throw me out of the cart. Metaphorically. I'd have to be like as much stronger than you than you are over normal people to turn you into my puppet. As powerful and stuff as I am, I can't even do that to a regular person, let alone you. <br /> <br /> &quot;The guy who told me this then went on about how in some rare cases the riding spirit and higher soul share the reigns, but that requires a deep spiritual bond and abiding trust and stuff. Then he went on about some stupid things about me and a primeval devourer blah blah blah legacy of Zem-nu blah blah blah something not seen since a anti-divulge-ian age... What's an anti-divulge-ian age? An age that people don't tell each other enough stuff? Because that pretty much describes now. &quot;<br /> <br /> Cinder pauses again, collecting himself after his latest tangent, &quot;the long and short of it is that I won't be able to control you, other than maybe shouting in your ears about whether to turn left or not. I'm going to do that anyway, but if we do this then I get around easier and you get to use some of my most miraculous divine powers. Win-win, right?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 06-30-2015, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:41:31-07:00","id":574802,"title":"","content":"Jensven chuckles at appropriate, and sometimes inappropriate times. However, he listens intently to the spritely little fire and does not interrupt. He only responds after the last question is presented to him.<br /> <br /> &quot;In case you haven't noticed, I already have miraculous divine powers,&quot; He starts. &quot;Also, I think you mean that you want to put your face in a palm, not the other way around. I believe things go in palms instead of in faces. Things in faces are generally not good.&quot; A short pause and then he gets more serious and introspective. &quot;I am so attached to this bag of muddy water because it is all I have. It is my home even more than any building could be. The thought of having that taken away from me is understandably very uncomfortable. I don't blame anyone else for that sentiment.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You are correct that I seem to have more mental and emotional strength than the average person. The Sun has given me gifts that I still do not understand the strength of. That said I will still have to think over what you have said. I won't be willing to let you ride me yet. I don't think I will ever let you ride Shadow. I value him the way he is. I don't want anything to change him other than what would naturally make him better in the same way he is a good companion now.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Dawn stops and gestures to the dog for his next point, &quot;Let's talk about dogs and cows. Shadow is a dog. He is an animal that is built to be a predator so he can eat. He would eat a cow if he could get away with it. I doubt he could kill a cow alone, but he might be able to do that. A few dogs like him and you definitely have a dead cow and well fed dogs.&quot; Jensven points to the dog's eyes and his ears, &quot;You see how he has eyes and ears that point ahead of him? This is so he can focus on what he wants to kill and eat. Thankfully, he doesn't have to worry about that. I get him all the food he can want. This way he can serve as my companion and sometimes pull heavy things through snow. His breeding has made him well suited to pulling sleds through snow.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Lawgiver starts to walk in the direction he believes Yi to be in as he moves on to the traits of bovine animals, &quot;A cow is much larger than Shadow. They also have shorter, less dense hair. The primary purpose of a cow is to serve as a means to get foodstuffs for humans. Whether they are milked, used for a plow, or slaughtered for meat. They have eyes and ears that are more to the sides of their heads so they can see and hear in a larger area than a predator. They also live in herds, large families if you want to think of it that way. This is so they have the safety of numbers for when wolves or other predators show up. Wolves are very much like Shadow, only more wild and less willing to obey commands. When predators do show up the cow doesn't necessarily need to be able to fight off or even outrun them. It just needs to be faster than at least one other cow. If the predators bring down the slower cow, this one lives another day.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you see the reasons we need different names for different four legged, furry things? They serve different purposes or do different things.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":1146,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","user":"Belkra","date":". 07-01-2015, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T11:36:00-07:00","id":576638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=567997#post567997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Wyld)<br /> <br /> &quot;Wha?&quot; The woman says to Amelia, &quot;Yes, of course. I'm only holding on to it 'cause the monster's scared of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> She cocks her head in response to Tirien's question. &quot;It's year 46 of the eleventh age, of course.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Amelia will pull her hand out of reach from the Young woman (or whatever it was).<br /> <br /> &quot;The eleventh age ? What are you ?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T11:33:48-07:00","id":577552,"title":"","content":"(Jensven)<br /> <br /> Cinder makes the verbal equivalent of a shrug, &quot;Eh. Your cart. And all that stuff with animals? It's all Seatongue to me.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T11:43:01-07:00","id":577557,"title":"","content":"(Wyld)<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm human, of course,&quot; the young woman says, puzzled. Something sparks in her eyes and she says, &quot;Oh! You're a barbarian. You don't know the history of the World. <br /> <br /> &quot;The First Age was when Pei-Seth made himself, the land and Time. The Second, when he begat Marle, who made the Sky. The Third, when Dannu took form and made the Sea. The Fourth, when Dannu and Pei-Seth begat Shef-Joryis who made Life. The Fifth, when Hei-Seth made war upon the others. The Sixth, when the Five of them remade the World after the destruction. The Seventh, when the Legions of Chaos invaded under the Brazen Imperator. The Eighth was when those with the Blood of the Five Gods built a wonderous civilization, until some of them were seduced by the Brazen Imperator, who stoked the Fires of the Great Devourer in their souls, making them mighty but wicked, and glowing with golden fire...&quot;<br /> <br /> The young woman's eye falls upon Amelia's Glorious Solar Saber and shrieks, crawling as far into the crevice as she can get. &quot;Wyld-Demon!&quot; she shouts, &quot;Anathema!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T06:02:32-07:00","id":579740,"title":"","content":"Oh, by the great blazing balls of the salamanders themselves, were they really doing this? Saffron had been chased out of a fair few towns by angry husbands and wives when their pea-brains got an inkling that the dark, golden stranger with quicksilver grace and too-clever copper eyes was something more than themselves, though they too had assumed him to be Raksha. Maybe he could exploit that here.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Calm yourself, love,&quot; he soothes. &quot;The nasty Anathema won't hurt you. Your mortal eyes can't see them, but this one has his faerie chains around her. You know that word. Faerie, fae, Raksha. The Wyld beasties that have let you live so far. Kept you nice and safe here. And this Wyld beastie's ensorcelled the Anathema to do you no harm. See, this other vision of loveliness isn't scared of her. She trusts me to keep the demon in check. So, will you let this&quot;\u2014he casts around for words to describe Tirien\u2014&quot;exemplar of majesty lay her human eyes and hands on that scepter, that our party might free you?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> It is mostly balderdash. Complete and utter lies. But it furthers the perception of the two Solars of him as Raksha and, if it works, it will calm the hysterical woman.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">5 dice from Manipulation+Presence. 2 successes.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5005,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","user":"HeavenlyThunder","date":". 07-06-2015, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T11:11:29-07:00","id":579986,"title":"","content":"Jensven shrugs himself, &quot;Just as long as you can remember this one is a dog and not a cow, it should be alright. Perhaps I can explain again and relate it to things you know so that you have a better chance of understanding it.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Dawn continues his search for Yi. It would appear there is no crowd around the city at this point and that makes it harder to find the Zenith. He will just have to rely on other methods.<br /> <br /> Without anything being said, Shadow perks up. &quot;Find Yi, Shadow!&quot; And with that, the dog is off. He doesn't bother to sniff the ground, but he does pause to catch something on the breeze from time to time. After the briefest pause, he heads off again in a direction that he believes the other Solar is in.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So, what does the puppy need to roll to try and find Yi, or is that not something you would expect him to be able to do in such a densely populated environment?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T22:14:44-07:00","id":584196,"title":"","content":"In the silent hour before the dawn Yi shivered, letting the world\u2019s breath flowing down the river refresh his spirit. When he walked, still aflame with radiance, he called out to those he knew waited in the shadows he cast. \u201cCome forth and do not hide yourselves like those ashamed. Fetch me flame and ready yourselves, this day you shall win glory worthy of song in after days.\u201d<br /> <br /> They went. Some with drawn knives, others readied improvised clubs, some skulking still between shadows; but they went. Such was the power of his voice and bearing that none questioned and none disobeyed. They returned, and his worm followed after for the breath of expectation rose from them. Then they set all together to work.<br /> <br /> Seven tripods he wrought of amber, bronze, and crystal flame and each set alight drank the flame they sheltered and gave it back in ripples of gold and white; ten whirled amphora of the river opal, drawn from the common shells scattered on the strand, and rosy quartz and he filled them with the golden wine pressed by the dawn into fragrant dew and ten bowls of water for every bowl of it would not have made it thin; twenty gleaming seas fashioned like lilies out of silver and glass and their span was not less than ten cubits; twelve full sets of gear for racing horses and they were set with sparks of iron upon stone as lesser men might deck their stuff with jewels and no horse that wore them would slack its pace for want of the thunder of hoofs behind it. Last, and with greatest care, he wove seven of the marriage veils which in local speech were called kredemnon. Seven secrets and seven spells he whispered in each as he made them, binding each into the threads as he did. To those who knew these were of greatest price, a great blessing to the city and a terrible and fateful burden was each to bear.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">CNNT + 2<sup>nd</sup> Excellency (5 successes)<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8845/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.rpnation.com/styles/rpnlogo12.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8845/view\" target=\"_blank\"> Oops! We ran into some problems. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8845/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.rpnation.com/dice/8845/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> 9 successes total. The results are of course exceptional. I would appreciate knowing about how much in hard cash equivalent I just ponied up.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T07:53:45-07:00","id":590205,"title":"","content":"Amelia raises an eyebrow in surprise at Saffron's blatant lie and face palm herself gently so as to not bash her own face in with her armored hand.<br /> <br /> &quot;Saffron is that suppose to calm the lady ? I heard better pick-up lines from a dead drunk. We are wasting time here.'' <br /> <br /> Amelia grabs Saffron shoulder and shove's him back before discarding her sword by throwing it away but still keeping the charm active. Showing her empty hands to the woman, Amelia sits in front of the crevice while still keeping her distance and tries to take her most calm tone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay now listen to me well because I will not repeat myself, we need that scepter to contnue on our quest and we will have it but how we aquire it is up to you, first option you can take a leap of faith and give us the scepter we take you home safe and sound, we are going to Mox-Utlo anyway so we might as well take you along for the ride drop you off and then be on our way or two we take it and we leave you here alone with the gardian (Amelia jerks a thumb in the direction behind her were the gardian is) so make up you mind quickly we are pressed for time I'm afraid. What do you chose ?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T18:45:13-07:00","id":592199,"title":"","content":"Tirien looks at herself in her war form and blinks. This Fae had a silver tongue, to be sure, although she supposed that worse could be said of something that most mortals would view in the lines of &quot;Ancient God to placate with sacrifices and hopefully she goes away&quot; to &quot;Oh, gods above, Wyld-beast, kill it with fire&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe we ought not to shake her around? It seems like she's had a hard time of it,&quot; Tirien muses. <br /> <br /> She rolls <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/9046/view\" target=\"_blank\"> 3 suxx</a> to recall anything about Moxe Ulto. <br /> <br /> (I also spent 16 of my 30 exp to raise my Lore. Turns out, for a nebbish, bookish woman, Tirien as she was couldn't even read. How abominable. Now she has a Lore of 3, which is more how I imagined her. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T15:28:22-07:00","id":595062,"title":"","content":"(Wyld)<br /> <br /> Tirien cannot recall anything of Moxe-Ulto. Even the libraries of House Ledaal can't have information in every little two-bit threshold kingdom! Judging from the girl's reflection of time, though, you can guess that their religion is likely a bastardization of Shogunate-Era Immaculate dogma, combined with elements of local spirit worship. L<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course it's a lie!&quot; the young woman says, &quot;The Anathema are servants of the Brazen Imperator, King of Faeries and Demons! Why would a Faerie imprison one of its allies?&quot;<br /> <br /> As Amelia grows close to the woman, she makes a punching motion towards the lawgiver. The strike stops well short of Amelia, and she can see the girl is holding her fist so tight her knuckles are white. It even looks like her nails have bitten into her palm, drawing blood...<br /> <br /> A wave of fire explodes from in front of the girl's hand. Once your eyes adjust to the fire, you see that the young woman's blood is flowing into the fire in an organic fractal, much like the branches of a tree. Or blood vessels. <br /> <br /> &quot;Step way from the entrance!&quot; She says with uncharacteristic resolve, &quot;I'm coming out.&quot; <br /> <br /> She coats the scepter in her own blood while you give her the room necessary to crawl out. She then does so, standing with an almost regal posture. <br /> <br /> &quot;I know this is probably a trick to get the scepter,&quot; she says, &quot;But you will take me to Moxe-Ulto as you swore. And if you trick me or try to take the scepter from me, my blood will light and melt the thing to slag.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T15:47:44-07:00","id":595070,"title":"","content":"(Novalesk)<br /> <br /> A host of wonders does Yi pull from the bosom of the earth, worth the ransom of a prince. Such wealth is a great gift to Origenes, a mighty addition to his treasure vaults. That his vaults have both opened to Yi twice, as both prophet and grandson, would have some question the sincerity of the gift. But that is they. Yi gets a feeling that, wherever his twice-adoptive grandfather is, he approves.<br /> <br /> It is there, at the great Temple of Origenes, that Jensven finds Yi. Whether Shadow could actually find Yi here by smell, or has simply associated the Lawgiver with large-scale public events is up for debate. A large crowd is at the temple, much larger than Yi has seen there yet. It would seem that there has been a upturn in piety lately. <br /> <br /> Well ,Jensven and Yi are together. What do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T09:12:55-07:00","id":597025,"title":"","content":"True to the request of his most trusted companion and master, Shadow weaves his way through the crowd in order to approach Yi. He only hesitates for a moment to check for children before pressing on. It is relatively easy for him to bound around, under, over, and through the people that are in his way. Before long the canine bundle of energy is standing a short distance away from Yi. He makes no noise, but he is upright and alert. His tail is a blur of black and white. His position leaves room for a person to stand just ahead of him and to his right.<br /> <br /> The Dawn finds it much harder to get through the crowd and makes slow progress. It will take him much longer to reach the other Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T16:41:54-07:00","id":597493,"title":"","content":"There was no mistaking Shadow for any other dog. Even if Yi hadn't recognized his appearance, the attitude of... comfort around a flaring anima banner was vanishingly rare among all living things. After seeing that nothing required his immediate attention he squatted down to bring himself face to face with the dog. No doubt the master would be along presently, but for now he felt like having a little fun.<br /> <br /> &quot;I have to warn you, I am more of a cat person myself. Mine always had the most frustrating yet endearing habit of sitting on whatever it was I needed to be working on and watching me. Don't worry though, I don't dislike you because of it. You have all the patience of a cat without that smug superiority that makes me feel like I am missing something obvious. Don't tell Jensven, but I like you better. Just keep that between us though.<br /> <br /> Do you mind if I scratch behind your ears? I don't know if we know each other well enough for a rump scratch, and besides that we are out in public.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T20:39:40-07:00","id":597757,"title":"","content":"The dog graciously accepts any and all affection Yi wishes to lavish on him. He doesn't roll to his back like he does with Jensven or Maia, but that could be because he is wary of the crowd more than any distrust of the Zenith. His tail, despite seemingly not able to do so, becomes even more of a blur.<br /> <br /> &quot;I see you found him, Shadow. At first when I had prepared to find you myself, I didn't see the crowd. I figured that where ever there is a crowd in this city, there you will find Yi.&quot; Jensven finally makes it to the other Solar and stands at the ready. &quot;I have prepared for the trip and I have brought along a little friend. You have met the little ball of fire called, Cinder. He says he can help keep Shadow from getting sick in the Hell Realm.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Northerner gestures to the many packs he is carrying, &quot;I have food for Shadow, Cinder, and myself. Also, water. as much as I could carry.&quot; He holds up what appear to be small saddlebags, &quot;Shadow will carry some water, too.&quot; The Dawn then shakes his head, &quot;I still do not think it will be enough.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T12:02:02-07:00","id":598596,"title":"","content":"Saffron privately makes an oath that the next time he tells such an abysmal lie, he'll sell his favorite bangle. Not the next time he tells an outrageous one, but the next time he crafts it so poorly. But even he has the common sense to back away from the entrance of the cave when the blood-fire comes pouring out. He supposes they could just kill her now, but few things lend themselves to such poetic descriptions as the inferno he's witnessed and he'll be damned if he composes any imagery that does less than perfect justice to it. That, of course, requires research. Speaking of which, he should probably do some on the Immaculate dogma and the Fae so he doesn't get tripped up again.<br /> <br /> But that can wait. &quot;As you wish, fair maiden,&quot; he croons in his best gallant gentleman's voice. &quot;A fool may serve whatever court holds power.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T06:48:00-07:00","id":599328,"title":"","content":"Barely able to contain her rage toward the woman Amelia thought about calling her blade back, cutting the woman down and just taking the scepter but the words of the sun resonate through her mind instantly, calming the storm of rage in her soul. With her mind now calm, Amelia looks at the frighten woman with kindness and steps back giving her some space.<br /> <br /> &quot;Very well you have a deal, now may we know your name ?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:15:38-07:00","id":610170,"title":"","content":"Tirien rolls her eyes at this sheer farce before her, and holds out her hand to assist the woman crawling out of the hole. <br /> <br /> &quot;There, there. We're not here for any malevolent reasons. We're scholars and explorers. Apparently, it has been.,..some time since you might have last seen your city. Such is the nature of the realm you're now in,&quot; She says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:01:41-07:00","id":611251,"title":"","content":"(Wyld)<br /> <br /> &quot;I gave my name,&quot; The young woman says, &quot;And it is Quickly Falls The Silverleaf. Now we are to be leaving.&quot;<br /> <br /> The girl makes a motion towards the entrance. Should you move towards the exit the dark beast sits upon its perch. It's baleful eyes glisten with hatred and vitriol, and are all a fixed upon your new companion. <br /> <br /> Will you attempt to pass?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:03:09-07:00","id":611253,"title":"","content":"(Novalesk)<br /> <br /> [If you care for me to move things along, I will, but it seems like Yi and Jensven are conversing so I won't for now.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:02:37-07:00","id":616674,"title":"","content":"Saffron sighs. &quot;I suppose we won't be able to avoid combat this time, will we?&quot; he asks no one in particular, resigned to the potential of death. &quot;Well, you may as well know this one isn't raksha, in case anyone had planned strategies around Fae Charms. I believe our new companion would know my kith as the Wretched, or some such epithet.&quot; He glances at Quickly Falls The Silverleaf. &quot;Will you be lending aid in this melee?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T21:11:41-07:00","id":617125,"title":"","content":"[I am alright with either. I will wait for input from Exthalion before proceeding either way, though.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T17:36:16-07:00","id":618245,"title":"","content":"&quot;The last time I went on a long journey I collapsed from hunger and heart after wearing out my shoes. I trust your preparations more than mine. Speaking of...&quot; He gestured over a pair of young men holding a bolt of some black, mirrored fabric. &quot;I will need your measurements. Possibly Shadows as well. I have studied the desert nomads of the south and learned a bit about the sorts of Robes there wear. This fabric is blessed with a charm of coolness which should further enhance its usefulness. I have seen dogs with something like a tunic over them, but I don't know if Shadow is comfortable wearing or being seen in such a thing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T09:11:45-07:00","id":619010,"title":"","content":"<b>&quot;</b>Shadow will wear anything I ask him to. He isn't concerned about appearances like us 'smarter' creatures are,&quot; the Dawn smirks at the remark.<br /> <br /> &quot;I thank you for the amount of thought you have given us. I am sure with the robes you mention we will use even less of the water I have brought. I think we may need more food and water for you if we are to expect you to last the five days you mentioned the trip would take. I would be willing to share what I have, but that means we need more still. I think that with you carrying a pack and me carrying the packs I have, we should have enough to get to the Hell City you mentioned. Getting back, though....&quot; Jensven shrugs causing the pack he has slung over his shoulders to shift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T07:44:09-07:00","id":621247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavenlyThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=616674#post616674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saffron sighs. &quot;I suppose we won't be able to avoid combat this time, will we?&quot; he asks no one in particular, resigned to the potential of death. &quot;Well, you may as well know this one isn't raksha, in case anyone had planned strategies around Fae Charms. I believe our new companion would know my kith as the Wretched, or some such epithet.&quot; He glances at Quickly Falls The Silverleaf. &quot;Will you be lending aid in this melee?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Having followed Quickly falls the silverleaf, Amelia glance's at the guardian and calls back her blade back to her hand and puts herself between Quickly falls the silverleaf and the guardian after listenning to saffron.<br /> <br /> &quot;She will do no such thing Saffron and neither will you. Here's the plan: Dero, Saffron you cover Teleri and Quickly falls and head for th exit and you don't stop until you have reached it, me and Tirien will take on the guardian and keep it busy, we will meet you back at Aurem's later. Anybody has an objection ?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T19:08:57-07:00","id":623858,"title":"","content":"Saffron's pride is rankled, but he nods, beaming. Let them die, if they will. He's happy to live to tell the tale. &quot;My lady Quickly Falls The Silverleaf, right this way, if you're so inclined. If not, I'm well-armed and your fire-raising ability would be highly useful.&quot; He gestures towards the exit, hoping she won't acquiesce. The soft warmth of the sun in his veins has begun to rise to searing heat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T23:33:37-07:00","id":635479,"title":"","content":"(Wyld)<br /> <br /> Silverleaf nods in agreement, and you set yourself up for the plan. However, you failed to account for the fact that the guardian demonstrated the ability to understand your speech, and could leap long distances in a single bound. <br /> <br /> The guardian leaps from its perch, and sets itself directly in front of the portal out of the treasure vault. One head glares at the collected exalts, as if in challenge, while the other remains fixed on your new compatriot. If you continue, it will almost certainly come to blows. <br /> <br /> If you chose to press forward, roll join battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T00:00:19-07:00","id":635486,"title":"","content":"(Novalesk)<br /> <br /> &quot;A more pressing concern perhaps, is how you intend to make the trek to the Demon City&quot; a resonant baritone echoes through the crowd. The voice is familiar Yi, but not Jensven, and it is not long before Yi spots the Druj Hadad, resplendent in his fine garb, bearing circlet upon his brow and blade at his side. Noting the size and puissance of the fallen ashura-king, the crowd splits to give him a wide berth as he continues. <br /> <br /> &quot;Do you perhaps know the locations of the Fifty-two secret gates of the Demon Realm? Or the thirteen secret roads into the Endless Desert? Clearly, it is within your power to call up the Citadel of Brass such that you may simply exit her halls here in Creation into those in Hell. Perhaps you will call upon the services of the Clouded Serpent-Blossom, that may devour you here and defecate you in hell? Or perhaps you know the sacred mudra that allows you to step though a mirror into the City of Mirrors? The ritual to step from a Shadow into the Shaodw of All, and powers sufficnet to save yourself from its corruption? The Four names of Lost Mabhaddoth that move you into the Formless aether beyond the worlds, and the Three that allow you to step back wherever you wish it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Lacking a definite reply, he caries on, &quot;Surely you bear a Key to the Brazen Gates. Or a Compass of the Endless Wastes? A Coral Figurehead to the Vitriolic seas? Or are you so completely and utterly arrogant that you think you can put upon mind-shattering depression and sorrow at a whim?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T17:12:55-07:00","id":637548,"title":"","content":"Saffron grits his teeth, before remembering his persona as an entertainer. It wouldn't do to break his role. He turns his grimace into a grin, fierce as a tiger's. &quot;My lady, I think we might be forced to dance with yonder guardian. I doubt that he, she, it, whichever will permit my words to reach it a second time. And to be entirely truthful, it's been far too long since I reveled in the song of blood and Essence.&quot;<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits+Awareness gave me five dice, which I rolled for three successes.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T12:25:25-07:00","id":640520,"title":"","content":"&quot;Lacking an alternative, most dreadful lord, I was just going to book passage with the Guild, pay an expediting fee, and send the tab to the minister of foolishly approving my travel expenditures in public. Surely one of your awful majesty has some far better method, but it is above my station to presume to ask you to make it available for a journey of my own request.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T16:18:25-07:00","id":640782,"title":"","content":"Tirien sighs, and assumes a fighting stance akin to what Mejan taught her, loose, with her weight on one foot, with the other ready to snap kick at a moment's notice.<br /> <br /> She rolls <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/10984/view\" target=\"_blank\"> one suxx</a> on join battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T19:52:47-07:00","id":641008,"title":"","content":"Once again, Jensven finds himself not understanding much of what people are saying around him. Once again, he refuses to be shamed by his lack of knowledge and vows to not let it hold him back. He would study up on these things that were mentioned (as many as he could remember anyway) when they returned from this Malfeas. He intends that to be a forgone conclusion as opposed to a mere possibility or even a likely outcome.<br /> <br /> The Dawn nods in assent at what Yi mentions as their intent for travel. As Shadow doesn't seem to be terribly interested or concerned with the new-comer, he will not be too guarded in his interactions with him. It is obvious he is no normal person, whatever he is. He does bear some attention if only to watch, listen, and learn about the ways of the strange things that were happening ever more rapidly to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":1146,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","user":"Belkra","date":". 08-26-2015, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T07:58:05-07:00","id":645427,"title":"","content":"Amelia assume a guard stance with her sword waiting for the beast to charge. (Rolls join battle with 9 dice for one <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/11159/view\" target=\"_blank\">suxx</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T17:21:04-07:00","id":650745,"title":"","content":"[Jensven and Yi]<br /> Hadad snorts at Yi's comment, saying, &quot;Humility ill becomes a king. It ill becomes you. Especially because I know it to be false.<br /> <br /> &quot;You have obtained the services of another of your ilk, and his war-beasts. This is good. You have also obtained victuals for the journey. This is also wise, for there is much in the realm of the Titans that is toxic to those raised in this bland age. While it would be amusing to see you trek across the Endless Wastes yourselves, either I would have to go with you or track you down afterwards, both of which are simply unacceptable. I shall allow you to travel with me, for I am a cruel and magnanimous monarch. As the chancellor has not yet called for the informant I require, we shall leave tomorrow at dawn. Meet me where the city's southern wall meets the waters. we shall travel from there.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hadad vanishes from your presence with a miniature thundercrack an a whiff of saline sea-air, leaving you to finish your preparations, and allowing Jensven and Shadow to be properly fitted for the cloaks made of Yi's hard-won magical cloth.<br /> <br /> [Yi, Jensven and Shadow obtain new magical cloaks, granting them +3 bonuses to resist Heat based effects]<br /> <br /> You arrive at the meeting place that Hadad gave you at dawn of the next day, but the druj is nowhere to be found. You wonder if you misheard Hadad, or perhaps he is running late, or even if he is deliberately fooling with you, as the sun begins to crest the eastern horizon. But, as the first sliver of the solar disk becomes visible, you hear a sucking sound in the river, and a long, crooked vessel wrought of verdigrised copper. Two banks of a dozen long metallic oars mar each side of the ship, and three masts, each with a single triangular azure sail line the vessel's deck. The towering figure of Hadad stands before a massive throne at the stern of the vessel, his hand upon a massive rod that leads to the ship's scale-like rudder. Hadad waves his hand, and a group of chained squalls lower a plank for you to board the ship.<br /> <br /> Hadad hardly waits for you to board before sitting upon his throne and jostling the rudder. As he does so, the ship shudders and lurches into the air. Bolts of lightning flash between the sails and the blades of the oars, but the Captain-king pays it no heed. It seems but a scarce moment before Novalesk is lost beneath you, and then but another more before the green sweetness of terra firma are lost amid the crystal blue of the clear sky.<br /> <br /> When you approach him, Hadad bids you to take whatever comforts you can in any of the cabins below decks, save the stern-most, and to help yourselves to the contents of his larder. The cabins are spartan at best, but they are dry and contain at least enough room for you to stow your goods and sleep. Hadad's larder, on the other hand, seems more a feast table than a ladder, with fine and bizarre dishes from every corner of Creation and the beyond.<br /> <br /> There does not appear to be any souls aboard the vessel save Hadad, Cinder, Shadow and the two solars, giving you full run of the vessel to train, spar, or do whatever thou wish to while away the hours of your five-day voyage. Hadad does not move from his throne, nor does his hand ever leave the rudder. He does not make conversation, and answers any questions as tersely as possible. Perhaps his full attention is required with the navigation, you think, it is best to not break his concentration.<br /> <br /> The voyage is mostly uneventful. Your ability to mark the passage of hours is hindered greatly by your inability to watch for the location of the sun or stars. After some time the azure sky fades to wine-dark, and then lightens back to azure. Twice more the cycle repeats, but each time the azure seems to leave shorter and the darkness return faster.<br /> <br /> Some time in the journey, before even the first transition of light to dark, you sail past a large hilled island floating among the sky. Lush verdant vegetation dots the surface, and you can see the ruins of a small city or fortress crumbling atop its surface. From what you can gather, the ruins penetrate even unto the lowest roots of the island, as it seems to have some form of man-made structure on the bottom as well.<br /> <br /> Shortly after light first fades to darkness, a long fifteen winged serpent, cloaked in feathers of saffron, cerulean, emerald, crimson and violet, comes alongside the ship. It dances in the air along the vessel's bow, much like a dolphin around a maritime ship. It makes no move to attack, and after some short time simply flies off to parts unknown.<br /> <br /> Towards the end of the second period of light, a crystalline javelin flies past the ship's starboard bow. Hadad makes no comment, but does change course a few points to port.<br /> <br /> In the deepest, darkest recesses of the third and final night, you pass a titan ghostly orb, bathed in violet light. The massive sphere covers the horizon, and fills you with existential dread. All the more terrifying, though, are the handful of dark shapes that orbit the violet sphere. Each is different if shape and size, but all of them defy conventional geometry and perspective, causing you pain simply by looking at them. What's more, as you draw past them, an ethereal sound penetrates your mind, as if coming from just beyond your range of hearing. It is simultaneously the most beautiful thing you have ever heard, surpassing even the radiant voice of the most high, and the most terrible. The pain from these cacophonous whispers are as if a thousand knives were being drawn across a hundred slates inside your heads. Passing this terrifying system is the only time in your journey that Hadad rises from his throne. Keeping a hand upon the rudder, he makes the lesser Mudra of the Rising Smoke at the violet orb until it is out of sight. Only then does he return to his seat. Any attempts to query Hadad about the nature of the place you just passed earn but one response, &quot;It is the place that the lost things go to die.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not long after this, the world around you begins to lighten, but not to the now-familiar azure. Instead, the sky begins to lighten to a soft emerald-green. Some time later, the vessel touches down in reeking, oily, green-grey sea. Upon the nearby shoreline, you can see a titanic city of brass, iron and lead. Black spires pierce up into the sky, and a molten sphere, burning with emerald fire, hangs above the brazen city. Even the most ignorant of occultists would be able to recognize the heart of the Demon Realm; the form of Ligier, the Green Sun.<br /> <br /> Hadad\u2019s ship crunches upon the shoreline of metallic beads. As you prepare to leave, Hadad rises from his throne and says, \u201cAs soon as you take foot from this ship, you will be within the Realm of Malfeas. Or Hell, as you Creation-born call it. Three things I warn you. First, bring not with you metals hewn from the earth and soil of creation. The Brazen Emperor does not suffer them to enter his gates; only when sorcery is placed upon them, or they are incorporated into an Artifact can they survive entry into the Demon Realm. Second, judge not based on what you can see. You are neophytes here. The logic of Creation is not the logic of the Yozis or of the Unquestionable. And third, always be on your guard. As Solars, to the Serfs you are walking disasters. To the Peers, you are an ally to be courted and corrupted, or a rival to be slain. And to the Unquestionable and the Titans, you are one of the most powerful Weapons of the Gods. They will attempt to steal you from your masters, or slay you if they cannot. Everyone and everything here will try to use you, slay you, or both.\u201d<br /> <br /> You debark Hadad\u2019s ship, followed by your elemental ally and demonic guide. Once you are all free and clear of the vessel, it sinks beneath the waves.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhere\u2019s it going?\u201d Cinder asks, concern in his voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cTo begin its five day journey to my home,\u201d Hadad replies, \u201cto await my summons for our return.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re stuck here for at least <i>ten days?</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course not,\u201d Hadad snorts, \u201cIt will arrive exactly when I summon it, having just spent the last five days sailing back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut,\u201d Cinder protests, \u201cIf you summon it, say, four days from now, then it will have had to have started its return trip yesterday. Before we even arrived. Before you sent it back to begin with.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know I don\u2019t get out much,\u201d Cinder says, \u201cbut that sounds impossible. Like, me playing the sanxian impossible.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs I said, the logic of the Creation-born does not apply here,\u201d Hadad says smugly.<br /> <br /> You now take stock of your surroundings, and two things spring out at you. First, is the air. It seems to light, to thin; almost as if you\u2019re standing atop a high mountain. But at the same time, it seems to exert a greater pressure upon you, akin to the increased pressure of being underwater. It does not hamper your movements, but it is disquieting.<br /> <br /> The second thing you notice is the noise, far more than simply being in a city can account for. All around you, you hear the pounding of drums, the blair of horns and simple yelling and shouting of demons of all shapes and sizes. a scarce minute after setting foot in Malfeas, a single piercing shriek from a thousand directions cuts through the din.<br /> <br /> It is dawn on your first day in the demon city. What shall you do?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T17:26:39-07:00","id":650753,"title":"","content":"[Wyld]<br /> <br /> (Well then. The Beast beats all of your Join battles, with a roll of Four successes. Dero gets two successes, and Sivlerleaf, one. <br /> <br /> So the Beast goes first. )<br /> <br /> The guardian beast sits, perched on its many wings, coiled, ready to react to a move to advance. A move to attack. It sits, clicking its razor fangs. But it does not move to attack.<br /> <br /> (In the words of Belkra, All that to say Guard. Guard like a foo.)<br /> <br /> Saffron's turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T20:58:18-07:00","id":652085,"title":"","content":"Saffron grits his teeth, masking it as a grin. To draw a blade might cost him his life if the beast takes it as provocation. Instead, he readies himself to hit the deck. Hopefully someone else dies first. (That is to say, Guard... I suppose with his Dodge DV, if it matters)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T09:05:32-07:00","id":656611,"title":"","content":"Jensven stares in dumbstruck wonder at the ship as Hadad makes his grand entrance. His composure fails to improve over the course of the journey and the Dawn can be seen to stare at all of the wondrous and terrifying happenings over the course of the journey. Shadow stares intently at the serpent creature, his posture stiff and poised to spring. However, as they pass the vast, ghostly orb the canine hides in a cabin below decks. Jensven is too preoccupied with keeping himself rational through this to retrieve the dog until the event has passed.<br /> <br /> The rest of the journey he spends training. Training alone with his steel blade, the sword Cinder, unarmed, or with Shadow. He even spars with Yi, should the Zenith request it. If anyone asks him to use his artifact blade he politely, yet stubbornly refuses with as few words as possible. When he is not training his body, the Northerner is training his mind. He chats at length with Cinder about all things artifact, steering the discussion to artifact armors as often as he can. Also, he can be seen to consult with Yi about politics, religions, and social concerns if the former Lookshan concedes to polite requests for conversation. It is readily apparent that he is attempting to fill in the holes he has found in his knowledge. It also becomes apparent that the more he learns the more he realizes he does not know. Then he can be seen to plunge forward in his pursuit of knowledge.<br /> <br /> On the morning of the arrival, he gets up early. He brushes out Shadow just like he has done for the other days of the trip. The excess fur is discarded over the rail of the ship. He then readies the packs for himself and the dog. Finally the cloaks are placed on both and they move topside to wait for their arrival. Jensven returns to his cabin when told that he cannot carry two of his blades with him. The Dawn places the steel blade of his own crafting and the sword Cinder in the cabin, and he keeps the artifact, Raija's Tears on his hip.<br /> <br /> &quot;I would rather I not have to draw this one,&quot; Jensven says to himself, even though the dog is always present and listening. &quot;To save myself or someone else, but never when I am the one attacking.&quot;<br /> <br /> With that he makes his way off the ship with the sled dog behind him. Both the Solar and his familiar seem to react the same way to the clashing, clanging din all around the city. Their ears move backward and they narrow their eyes. Shadow manages to get his ears flat to his head, and he is very uneasy, casting his gaze about warily. His master seems only slightly less ill at ease. His gaze casts about, but more like one that is on guard than one that is expecting to be attacked at any moment.<br /> <br /> It is in this manner they wait to see what will happen and where it is recommended they should go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T15:51:36-07:00","id":668903,"title":"","content":"[Wyld] <br /> <br /> (Well, then. It's now Dero's turn.) <br /> <br /> Dero stands on guard, glittering bronze knives prepared in his hands. The golden warrior told him to wait and guard the strange blood-fire lady. And If Dero learned anything growing up, its that it's a very bad idea to disobey such a fiercely assertive woman. At least when you're within their reach. <br /> <br /> (Dero guards. It's now Amelia, Tirien, Silverleaf and the Beasts' turns).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T18:38:00-07:00","id":669106,"title":"","content":"[Malfeas]<br /> <br /> You pause, taking stock of the particular circle of Hell you have landed within. From what you can see, the city before you is heavy disorganized, with building being of wildly varying sizes, from mere shacks to domiciles that rival the size of Lookshy Manor. There is no rhyme or reason with their shapes either, with some being cylindrical or spherical, others being a mess of acute angles and far-to-many walls, and the (very) occasional one having the right angles and flat surfaces you've come to expect in human construction. Black lead, dull iron and bright brass fuse together, adding the the visual confusion. <br /> <br /> Hadad scoffs, &quot;Such disorganization. The peer who rules this section of the city is weak. Sloppy. Complacent. So disorganized.&quot; He gestures at a tall, sharp, lead spire. You can make out a trio of crude hoof-prints pressed into its surface. &quot;Just because your territory abuts a natural barrier, you have no defenses? No garrison? The fool.<br /> <br /> &quot;Still this works to our advantage,&quot; Hadad says, &quot;We must make our way to the Plain of Teeth. Therein lies a tower of marble and glass: the Eyrie of the Watcher. You shall find the Relic there. Unfortunately,&quot; Hadad says, with the first hint of apology in his tone you've ever heard, &quot; the geography of the Demon City has changed since the crumbling of my glorious empire. I navigated us as closely as possible to the Plain, but I know not whether it is above us, or below. We must learn of any information the denizens know of the Tyrant K'rishar, or of Tegus the Nine-Fold, the Plain of Teeth. Those queries are most likely to point us towards your goal.<br /> <br /> &quot;And, I might add,&quot; Hadad says, any and all apology gone from his voice, &quot;That I still bear a resemblance to the Peers of Hell. While that may open doors to us, <i>me</i> asking those questions will undoubtedly raise far more questions than I'm comfortable with. You will have to do the vast majority of the 'leg-work' as it were.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T10:25:18-07:00","id":669840,"title":"","content":"Without hesitation Amelia charge's the monster her blade in hand feinting a charge before jumping toward it as if trying to jump on the creature, swinging her blade in the empty air as she jumps toward the monster, Solar essence can be seen crackling along the edge of her sword as her swing release a powerful arc of deadly solar essence speeding toward the creature, following not far behind Amelia comes in for the kill aiming to thrust her blade deep into the creature's back using her fall to add speed and additional strength to her second strike.<br /> <br /> (Amelia makes two attacks and a jump/move action her first attack uses Iron raptor technique 4m, hungry tiger technique 1m and first melee excellency for 3m adding 3 dice, her second attack use hungry tiger technique 1m and first melee excellency for 8 motes for 8 dice. Total 17 motes of personnal essence, no motes of personnal essence remains. First attack (17-3+3=17 dice) scores <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/12067/view\" target=\"_blank\">7 suxx</a>, second attack (17-4+8=21 dice) scores <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/dice/12068/view\" target=\"_blank\">7 suxx </a>. Both attack has a base damage of 15L/2)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 09-18-2015, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T10:40:39-07:00","id":683276,"title":"","content":"&quot;There was one thing I had hoped to ask on the way, though now is as good a time as any. Is there any... resentment is close enough toward the chosen of the gods here? If we came in force of arms and soul sundering might I suppose no one would make an issue of it. As it is, we are young and I am not the invincible fury of the dawn. Should we refrain from revealing our nature, or at least flaunting it? Would we be better served by appearing to be in your service? Assuming we go into very little detail of course.<br /> <br /> Essentially, how should we conduct ourselves.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T18:46:05-07:00","id":689083,"title":"","content":"Jensven will add his thoughts to Yi's question after it is voiced, &quot;I would say that we avoid armed conflict if possible. However, the Dawn that was has told me that I don't need to be armed with steel in order to be armed. I agree that we should hide what we are unless it is impossible. We are here for the item. We get it while making as little noise as we can and then we leave.&quot;<br /> <br /> His gaze is still scanning the area just beyond their landing point as he speaks. He speaks bravely, but he seems very much on edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T16:37:47-07:00","id":690594,"title":"","content":"Tirien will observe the beast, concerning itself with it's movements and behavior, something nagged at the back of the Lunar's mind.<br /> <br /> &quot;This isn't some feral beast. We've been lied to, I think, &quot; she muses , preparing for her next move.<br /> <br /> Tiriem will make an aim action on the beast by observing it , for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T20:00:29-07:00","id":694454,"title":"","content":"(Wyld)<br /> <br /> Amelia's two strikes hit home, causing the beast to recoil in shock and pain. A whip of fire lashes out from Silverleaf, and rakes the Beast. It retreats, shrinking towards the exit, continuing to block the doorway, but still taking no steps to attack.<br /> <br /> Saffron's turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T11:17:14-07:00","id":696295,"title":"","content":"(Malfeas)<br /> <br /> &quot;There are benefits and detriments to both hiding or revealing your natures,&quot; Hadad says, &quot;Hiding your natures will draw less attention, true. But the attention you do draw will undoubtedly be hostile, as your kind are viewed as chattel by my erstwhile kindred. And even the least among the Princes of the Earth are forces to be feared among demon-kind. It could serve you well to flaunt your nature, should you accept the proper poise and demeanor.<br /> <br /> &quot;As to appearing in my service, it depend on whether you flaunt or hide your nature. If you hide, that is likely the best course. The Peers are able to seduce the scions of Creation's gods with ... regularity. But if you flaunt your nature appearing in my service would raise too many questions. Those Peers who are able to place even one of the chose of the celestines under their thrall are few and far between. If that is the choice you take, I will simply be your guide.&quot; Hadad shrugs, &quot;It is true enough.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T15:20:23-07:00","id":696542,"title":"","content":"How infuriating. The creature has retreated. Far less drama to that than if it had advanced and given them a last-stand ending. Saffron supposes that he'll make up for it with his most beautiful weapon-- one of his jeweled knives. He lunges for the beast and, with an expert flourish of his blade and a mesmerizing whirl of flame-colored silk, slashes the glittering edge of the blade across its underbelly like a ship's prow parting water.<br /> <br /> (Spoiler mechanism is glitching so here goes: move action on first attack. Hungry Tiger Technique used (1 m) and Second Melee Excellency (6 m) to add 3 suxx. Counts as 6 extra suxx I think. (6+1=7 m of personal essence expended). Roll of (Dex+Melee+Specialty) is (4+2+1) is 7 dice for 2 suxx. Bracers allow him a 2 die bonus for 1 success. 9 in total. Base damage of 4L (weapon damage+Strength.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}